# =============================================================================
# .gitattributes
# =============================================================================
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS:
#   Windows ends lines of text with two invisible characters (CRLF), while
#   macOS and Linux use one (LF). When a team mixes operating systems, Git can
#   show every line of a file as "changed" just because the line endings flipped.
#
#   This file tells Git how to handle files, no matter what each person's
#   computer settings are. Here we make every text file use LF, which matches
#   the `end_of_line = lf` rule in .editorconfig.
# =============================================================================

# Auto-detect text files and always store/check them out with LF endings
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touch their contents
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
